spruce works out the order of operators from the path as written, mm.$GRAFT_T_XX.v, and replaces $GRAFT_T_XX only when the concat at aa runs. So it does not know that aa reads mm.ab.v, it runs aa first because aa sorts before mm, and it writes aa: x-(( concat "a" "b" )) with exit code 0. graft replaces $NAME with the variable's value when it parses the reference, so the dependency on mm.ab.v is known before anything runs, and it writes aa: x-ab.
